    "problem_statement": "QR code generation fails with UnboundLocalError on variable 'dark'\n\nWhen trying to generate QR codes, the library throws an `UnboundLocalError: local variable 'dark' referenced before assignment` error. This happens for any QR code generation, making the library completely unusable.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('Hello World')\nqr.make()\n```\n\nThis simple example that should work according to the documentation fails with:\n\n```\nUnboundLocalError: local variable 'dark' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThe same error occurs when trying to generate images:\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('test data')\nimg = qr.make_image()\n```"
